roduced a number of convenience  structures they're convenient  constructors associated with granularity  so we have current next and previous  dates which take a granularity and  optionally a reference date so if I want  to know what month it is I can evaluate  current date of month or what year it is  current date of year and it will give me  the granular step associated with the  current timestamp so if I want next year  I can say next date of year or I can  give a reference date for previous date  and say I want to know what week was  before Wednesday April 3rd of 2013 and  it will give me a granular object that  is a week beginning on Monday as our as  our week granularities canonically do  and it will take it in reference to that  original input date this is generalized  in terms of handling granularity and we  also allow day types so for version 12  we're introducing support for day types  where weekend day reference is a day  granular object but it has criteria  associated with it so I want the next  day that falls on a weekend or I wanted  the previous Wednesday or I want the  next Saturday I can generate the same  value but Sunday I can generate a  granular object with reference to the  specific criteria that's implied by that  day type you can also do convenient  calculations like if I want to know what  the weekday immediately preceding  Thanksgiving is I can provide a  reference date and then say the criteria  is I want what it to be a weekday we  also support comparisons between  granular data objects so for example I  can test either through sorting or  strictly by comparison that today  precedes tomorrow or I can ask is today  the same thing as now and equal  understands that the granularity step  means that now falls within the period  of today so there's not really an  equivalence test that we could give a  true or false to so in this case we give  a warning message and we return on  evaluated one of the ways we can handle  that is that we include 